# zoo_0000 interact-turn dispatch - CHTPM-MODULE VARIANT, PERSISTENT
# LOOP.
#
# REVERTED BACK TO PERSISTENT (2026-07-19, see xyzos-standards.txt sec.
# 0-CORRECTED and yz.muchiverse/2.muchi-verse/agent-b-notepad.txt for
# the full investigation): this file's own one-shot conversion (paired
# with chtpm_parser_pal.c's own then-new run_module_synchronous() - a
# BLOCKING fork+exec+waitpid call on the "Control Zoo" onClick=
# "INTERACT" button) hangs the entire chtpm_parser_pal process the
# instant any key is pressed while "in control", the same live-caught
# bug egg-pals-13's own main_loop_chtpm.pal had (see that file's own
# header comment for the full account - identical root cause, same
# fix). Direct re-check against real 1.TPMOS's own chtpm_parser.c
# (line 2878) confirmed its own INTERACT handling is plain, fire-and-
# forget inject_raw_key() - no wait, no fork from that function at all;
# reverted at the source (shared-ops/chtpm_parser_pal.c). With that
# fixed, this file goes back to a genuine PERSISTENT loop, matching
# real fuzz-op_manager.c's own architecture (a persistent daemon with
# its own independent poll thread, not a one-shot script re-forked per
# keystroke) and this family's own wsr-pal/pal-chain precedent.
#
# WHY interact_relay.txt, NOT history.txt LIKE fuzz-op's <interact> TAG:
# real TPMOS's own raw keyboard capture writes ONLY to
# pieces/keyboard/history.txt - chtpm_parser.c is the SOLE writer of
# whatever file a project's own <interact src="..."> names. This
# family's shared-ops/keyboard_input.c is NOT single-purpose the same
# way - it ALSO writes every raw keystroke directly and unconditionally
# to pieces/apps/player_app/history.txt, for projects whose own regular
# non-chtpm "run" mode still reads that file via prisc+x's read_history
# op. interact_relay.txt is never touched by keyboard_input.c - only
# chtpm_parser_pal's own inject_raw_key() (INTERACT branch) writes to
# it, restoring the single-writer guarantee fuzz-op gets for free from
# real TPMOS's own narrower raw-capture design.
#
# chtpm_parser_pal's own menu nav (arrows/digits/Enter before "Control
# Zoo" is engaged, and ESC to return to it afterward) is unaffected by
# any of the above either way - it's driven entirely by chtpm_parser_pal
# reading pieces/keyboard/history.txt directly inside its own process_key(),
# never by this file's own read_history line.
#
# compose_rgb_frame is NOT called here: it draws real 2D tile graphics
# straight from game-state files and never touches current_frame.txt -
# button.sh's own "run" action launches system/chtpm_rgb_render
# alongside chtpm_parser_pal, a separate, persistent daemon that
# font-rasterizes current_frame.txt itself (chrome AND embedded game
# map, verbatim) into the SAME rgb_frame.raw gl_mirror reads. Calling
# compose_rgb_frame here too would overwrite that daemon's own output
# with the OLD chrome-blind tile view on every run.
li x1, 0

compose_frame
hit_frame

loop:
read_history pieces/apps/player_app/interact_relay.txt x2, x1
beq x2, x0, no_key
xlector_input x2
tick_pets
compose_frame
hit_frame
j loop

no_key:
sleep 30000
j loop
